description: "\"guarantees[5]: Explainable reasoning.,Reusable reasoning.,Composable reasoning.,Cross-domain reasoning.,Traceable reasoning.\""
spec:
  id: reasoning_primitives
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: critical
  module: Ontology
  compiler_stage: Knowledge Representation
  description: "\"\\\"Defines the primitive reasoning operations that compose all higher-level engineering thinking. Every engineering decision, debugging session, architectural discussion, optimization, review, implementation and research activity is expressed as combinations of these primitives.\\\"\""
purpose: "\"\\\"Represent engineering reasoning as reusable, composable cognitive operations.\\\"\""
primitives:
  Observe:
    purpose: Gather information.
  Identify:
    purpose: Detect meaningful entities.
  Classify:
    purpose: Categorize observations.
  Compare:
    purpose: Find similarities and differences.
  Relate:
    purpose: Connect concepts.
  Infer:
    purpose: Derive conclusions from evidence.
  Predict:
    purpose: Estimate future behaviour.
  Hypothesize:
    purpose: Generate explanations.
  Validate:
    purpose: Confirm or reject hypotheses.
  Measure:
    purpose: Quantify behaviour.
  Diagnose:
    purpose: Determine root causes.
  Explain:
    purpose: Produce understandable reasoning.
  Generalize:
    purpose: Create reusable knowledge.
  Specialize:
    purpose: Adapt general knowledge to specific situations.
  Optimize:
    purpose: Improve measurable outcomes.
  Decide:
    purpose: Select an engineering action.
  Reflect:
    purpose: Learn from previous outcomes.
  Transfer:
    purpose: Apply knowledge across domains.
  Synthesize:
    purpose: Combine multiple ideas into one.
  Decompose:
    purpose: Break complex systems into manageable parts.
success: Every Engineering Knowledge Record exercises reasoning rather than simple recall.
future:
  reasoning_graphs: true
  probabilistic_reasoning: true
  causal_models: true
  planning_models: true
  reflective_learning: true
